polaris_scientist: paper prompts and skills

The Markdown prompts, the skill folders (SKILL.md files, scripts and templates)
and the licence text in this folder are derived from AI-Scientist-v3
(https://github.com/SakanaAI/AI-Scientist-v3), Copyright 2026 Sakana AI,
which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The licence is in the
file LICENSE in this folder.

The files were changed. Every Markdown file and every Python or shell script
carries a two-line header with the path of its original (relative to the root
of AI-Scientist-v3) and the list of its changes. The list below repeats the
changes in one line per file. JSON files cannot carry a header, so their
changes are listed here only. Where a line says "none", the file is a copy of
the original with a header only (or, for JSON, a plain copy).

Changes common to the prompts: the memory protocol, the global memory input,
the rubrics section, the contributions scaffold, the paper edit context, the
orchestrator-rendered concept figure steps and every use of image-model or
API-key context were removed; paths now use the placeholders of the phase
vocabulary and the inputs/, outputs/ and skills/ layout; the final_evaluation
paragraph was rewritten for the paper_data.json of this system. In the writer,
editor and write-paper-standalone files the advice to install tools and pandas
became the rule to use only what is already installed, because the agent has no
network.

Prompts (original under src/prompts/ in AI-Scientist-v3)
- reference_query_plan.md (reference_query_plan.md): removed the rubrics section, the global memory line and block, and the memory protocol.
- paper_strategy.md (paper_strategy.md): rewrote the final_evaluation paragraph, removed the study-field paragraph, the rubrics, the edit context section, the contributions scaffold, the memory protocol, the edit-mode fields and rules 17 to 19; the final prompt family is the name paper_standalone; the generator list has no concept-figure generator.
- posthoc_ranking.md (paper_posthoc_ranking.md): removed the rubrics section; the inlined analyses became a pointer to posthoc_analyses in paper_data.json and the files under dossier/posthoc/; the output path is a placeholder.
- paper_standalone.md (paper_standalone.md): used by the writer and the enricher; added a Working Folder section, which also says that create_file does not replace a file and how to replace a copied one; removed the study-field paragraph, the source evidence pointer, the rubrics, the memory protocol, the contributions scaffold, the global memory and image-model lines and the concept figure steps; rewrote the posthoc bullets, the Data Schema section and the source id convention; adapted the author block rule to a file that holds the whole \author command. Added the Printed numbers section (every number the paper prints is backed by a claim and a recorded value or derivation), the source id families task.constants and program.constants and the values of post-hoc data sources, and the baseline provenance. Added the paragraph and the data schema line that name the staged specification, source diff and verification record of each ablation variant and the control, and the rule that a description of a variant must agree with them.
- paper_reference_gaps.md (paper_reference_gaps.md): removed the global memory line.
- reference_query_plan_postdraft.md (reference_query_plan_postdraft.md): removed the global memory line.
- evidence_audit.md (paper_review/evidence_audit.md): rewrote the final_evaluation paragraph, removed the study-field paragraph; the audit packet is the paper snapshot folder; removed the retry-feedback files (a sentence about the task prompt replaces them); the text reply contract is unchanged. Added the paragraph that checks each description of a baseline, an ablation variant or the control against its staged specification, source diff and verification record, one line for it in the audit standard and a second failing example; the original has no wording for this.
- review_json.md (paper_review/review_json.md): same changes as evidence_audit.md; the review is a reply in the final message, so the Must write section and the review JSON path were dropped; the JSON contract is unchanged.
- paper_revision.md (paper_revision.md): added a Working Folder section, with the same create_file note; the inputs name the repair feedback, review feedback, evidence audit and current paper snapshot; removed the study-field paragraph, the source evidence pointer, the scope audit outputs and the scope audit JSON contract. Added the Printed numbers section (every number the paper prints is backed by a claim and a recorded value or derivation), the source id families task.constants and program.constants and the values of post-hoc data sources, and the baseline provenance. Added the paragraph on the staged files of each ablation variant and the control, and the rule for fixing a finding about the description of a variant.
- paper_edit.md (paper_edit_standalone.md): used by the editor; same changes as paper_standalone.md; in addition removed the scope audit outputs, the whole Method Scope Audit Contract section, the compatibility audit item, requirements 13, 15, 16 and 17, and the edit context bullets that depend on staged new-program inputs. Added the Printed numbers section (every number the paper prints is backed by a claim and a recorded value or derivation), the source id families task.constants and program.constants and the values of post-hoc data sources, and the baseline provenance. Same variant files paragraph and data schema line as paper_standalone.md.

