Script checks
All vendored scripts use only the Python standard library or the shell. None
imports from the original repository, none uses a repository-root path, none
uses the network. compile_latex.sh and validate_rendered_si.py call the
external commands pdflatex, bibtex and pdftotext, which must be on PATH.

New files
- NOTICE (this file).
- ../../venues/iclr/author_block.tex and ../../venues/iclr/NOTICE are new (see the NOTICE in assets/venues/iclr).

Original files left out
- agents/skills/generate-concept-figure: needs an image model and API keys, which are not available.
- agents/skills/memory-log: there is no memory system.
- agents/skills/retrieve-references: the agent has no network; the host retrieves references.
- agents/skills/write-paper: the standalone variant is used instead. Only its claims_grounding.schema.json and its templates/iclr files were taken (the latter are in assets/venues/iclr).
- agents/skills/write-paper/templates/alife: another venue.
- agents/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py: imports src.orchestrator modules of the original repository and cannot run alone.
- All other prompts of src/prompts: not used by this phase.
